  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nAs a Nor'easter spins near New England today, broad suppressed\nridging over the Gulf Coast and Southern Plains is still the\ndominant feature in our region. Latest guidance supports the \nridge building more directly overhead into next week as a cut off \nlow and remnants of current East Pacific Hurricane Polo affect the\nDesert Southwest region. With it appearing that the ridge may \nhold on more resolutely, the slower range of guidance with regards\nto advancing this low/trough to the east look more likely. \nOfficial guidance has POPs returning to parts of the area on \nWednesday, but slower eastward movement could push appreciable \nrain chances to late week or even the weekend. That will also be \nwhen a surge of tropical moisture moves in from the Caribbean, so \nwe could be setting up for heavy rainfall with a slow moving front\nin the region. Continue to look for updates as we move to the \nlater half of next week if hazardous severe weather or heavy \nrainfall and flash flooding become possible. /NF/",
